      "verification": "WAEC Ghana (BECE for school candidates) states a nine-point numerical scale with Grade 1 the highest performance and Grade 9 the lowest; no percentage range was found in any fetched WAEC or GES document, so the grades are entered results, not computed from a mark. The band's points are the reverse of the grade (grade 1 is 9 points, grade 9 is 1 point) because the best-n operator keeps the highest values; the BECE aggregate is 60 minus the best six points. The descriptors name only the highest and the lowest grade."
    }
